cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it as below."
title: "revision-bench: measuring revision-loop dynamics in large language models"
abstract: >-
  Measurement infrastructure for iterative LLM revision of prose. Controlled revision
  loops over a fixed corpus, instrumented with stylometric, lexical and blinded-preference
  readouts, scored per round, with pinned seeds, bootstrap confidence intervals and full
  provenance. The research question is under what acceptance architecture iterative
  revision is non-degrading while still fixing real defects.
type: software
# Alias only, matching the sibling mirror-bench repo. Do not substitute a personal name
# here: it was written that way on purpose, and an earlier draft of this file guessed one
# from the GitHub handle.
authors:
  - alias: skulitom
    website: "https://github.com/skulitom"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/skulitom/revision-bench"
keywords:
  - large language models
  - iterative refinement
  - stylometry
  - authorship attribution
  - text degradation
  - evaluation
version: 0.0.0.dev0
date-released: "2026-08-11"
